{
	"Name": "AlertQuery - Okta - User - MFA - Potential Okta MFA Bombing via Push Notifications [table]",
	"Description": "Finds accounts sent a burst of MFA push notifications, especially where the user denied some. MFA fatigue attacks work by holding a valid password and hammering the push prompt until the victim taps approve to make it stop, so a high push count with denials in it is the attack in progress.\n\nThresholds: 5 or more push sends, or 2 or more explicit denials, per account. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune them.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_potential_okta_mfa_bombing_via_push_notifications/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_potential_okta_mfa_bombing_via_push_notifications.toml",
	"GUID": "8a188024-aec5-5258-b6d2-68ab8941c403",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
